# Copy this to `.scan-identity` (gitignored) and list the identifiers that are
# YOURS: drive names, account handles, machine names. One per line, "#" comments.
#
# Why this file exists. `scripts/scan_repo.py` already catches any PATH-SHAPED
# personal literal: /Users/<you>/, /Volumes/<your-drive>/, and so on. What it
# cannot reliably catch is a bare name with no path around it, as in "the
# <drive-name> volume must be mounted". It tries, by reading the names of volumes
# that are mounted right now, but unplug the drive and the check silently stops
# working. Declaring the names here makes it deterministic instead.
#
# Entries shorter than four characters are ignored, as are common words like
# "root" and "runner", because a guard that fires on ordinary prose gets muted.
#
# This file is gitignored and must stay that way: it is the one file in the
# repository that names a specific person's things.
#
# Examples, replace with your own:
#
# MyBigAudioDrive
# my-laptop-hostname
# my-account-handle
